diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md
index 3eec54795..58326183a 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md
@@ -2825,6 +2825,10 @@ It seems not important anymore or urgent to fix the cause (religious dogpile) as
 
 As for this change of seemingly much better"emergency peace" prechecks, AI should be much stronger as well thanks to these hopefully and possibly be better at keeping its lead while still keeping the ability to bully the weak (i.e. many weak players) in multi wars for its interest (e.g. shortly before turn 200 hastsheput ai goes at it again and declares war on pacal 2 ai who was dying anyway and who is nearby so nice gain for her and safe as well).
 
+**Update:** Save-file 450 BBAI testing showed the original AdvCiv-SAS emergency override was too broad. It could force peace against every opponent and treated any three wars as an emergency even when all enemies together contributed only 70% effective power. It now selects only the lowest-value war whose opponent will negotiate, preserving better wars, and compares a tunable adjusted danger score against the existing 160% threshold. Each front beyond two raises actual combined enemy power by 25%, so numerous nearly powerless enemies cannot cause panic peace.
+
+The confirming run showed Sumer continue safely at three to four wars while capturing Ecbatana, Memphis, Boston, Thebes, and Baghdad. Only when a fourth front raised its 126% raw combined enemy power to 189% adjusted danger did it end one lower-value war, then it retained the others. This preserves KI#65's protection against real dogpiles without surrendering profitable wars merely because of their count.
+
 ## 66 - (Fixed and greatly enhanced) AI overvaluing bonuses that give minor effects such as pig or cattle/cow (+1 health only), etc, that AI would value the same as maize or wheat (+2 health effectively since almost all cities have a granary and very early) or grapes (from grocer) or molluscs (from harbor) for example, by adding a pre-check in CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal to value relatively more bonuses the more effects they provide from buildings if we have their required tech of these buildings, so that humans can't abuse/exploit it with aggressive trading to become super rich xd, and also in AI vs AI trading each AI gets best or more value out of the effective value of their bonuses at least more so now
 
 Screenshots/files for this issue: [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/13hSTVD9mOWRkaCnS3Z21s-8tbYaBr3Sf?usp=sharing).
@@ -6846,6 +6850,8 @@ The same final run was therefore the after-fix Lincoln branch, not a Lincoln win
 
 Fixed/improved with the help of GPT-5.5 (on ChatGPT Codex) thanks.
 
+**Update:** A later diagnostic run found 57 peace deals that `AI_negotiatePeace` reported as successful even though the final AdvCiv-SAS victory-denial guard kept the teams at war. The guard ran after deal logging and trade-value processing, so UWAI could repeatedly propose an ineffective treaty after already clearing its war state. The shared victory-threat check now blocks ordinary peace earlier in UWAI, `AI_negotiatePeace`, and final deal processing while leaving capitulation available. Confirming runs recorded zero false peace successes.
+
 ## 184.2 - (Fixed/Improved) UWAI Space victory-denial could still start too late when stage-3 Space leaders already had many spaceship parts before countdown
 
 Screenshots/files for this issue: [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sbQXIw23MagHuJcdzoCugLR8iX2_cMp4?usp=sharing).

diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index be4e10664..edff5d3a4 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -184,6 +184,7 @@ Note: cultural victory bullets as of now assume 3 legendary cities are required,
 Note 2: AI victory stages are internal AI strategy markers per victory route (`AI_VICTORY_*1` to `AI_VICTORY_*4`); stage 4 means a late/near-completion push. A victory countdown means the AI has an active turns-to-win estimate/launch countdown. UWAI war preparation means the AI has selected `WARPLAN_PREPARING_*` rather than declaring immediately; this can be too slow when a rival is close to winning.
 
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6038+) **AI victory denial is much more urgent:** BBAI testing in save file 450 showed a deep UWAI issue that UWAI could let a rival close to winning survive too easily: in the Lincoln runs, Lincoln was very weak militarily (~0.7 military power) but still won Space despite much stronger nearby AIs (up to ~2.1) and no war declared on him in the checked late-game snapshots (`wars=-` at T260, T270, T280, T290, then wins Space at T292); in the Ramesses runs, Ramesses was militarily strong (top 2 at ~1.9 vs ~2.1 for top 1) and likewise won Space without being at war in the checked late-game snapshots either (`wars=-` at T260, T270, T280, then wins Space at T290). After fixing the missing-war response, follow-up tests exposed additional failure modes: war could start too late, start but end after 1-2 turns through ordinary peace deals, or happen without enough impact. The decisive checks in this fix are now therefore low-level enough, because higher-level targeted patches did not reliably solve the observed chain of failures (similar in spirit to the AdvCiv-SAS scrapping or `AI_chooseUnit` final guards): in `UWAI::Team::scheme` and related functions. The fix now boosts war utility for stage-4/countdown victory threats, can convert that into direct war when the target is weak and near enough, and refuses ordinary peace while the target remains a serious victory threat. In the final Lincoln-branch retest, Lincoln was weak at T260 as usual (4 cities / 55 military units / 1818 power), but this time Persia, Egypt, France, and Babylon declared at T267-T269, peace was blocked, and America was eliminated at T272. In the separate Ramesses-branch retest, strong Ramesses still survived, but was no longer ignored: he lost 2 cities, 49 city-population points, 28 total units / 30 military units, and about a quarter of his power from T260 to T290. The direct-war gates stay intentionally narrow so distant or naval-heavy threats can receive utility pressure without forcing reckless cross-map attacks. See [KI#184](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#184---fixedimproved-multiple-uwai-victory-denial-issues-could-let-imminent-space-winners-survive-no-war-before-fixing-this-regardless-of-whether-ai-was-very-strong-militarily-like-in-the-ramesses-run-or-very-weak-like-in-the-lincoln-run-then-even-after-the-initial-fix-wars-were-still-too-late-too-short-or-too-low-impact).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6053+) Update: Follow-up diagnostics found 57 cases in which an AI tried to make ordinary peace with a rival close to victory. The earlier AdvCiv-SAS fix kept the war active as intended, but didn't take into account that UWAI had already accepted the peace treaty internally even though the teams remained at war: the SAS rejection was too late in the process. To fix this, these treaties are now rejected before UWAI processes them, so its decisions and logs correctly show that the war continues; capitulation remains available, and confirming runs had zero false peace successes. See [KI#184](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#184---fixedimproved-multiple-uwai-victory-denial-issues-could-let-imminent-space-winners-survive-no-war-before-fixing-this-regardless-of-whether-ai-was-very-strong-militarily-like-in-the-ramesses-run-or-very-weak-like-in-the-lincoln-run-then-even-after-the-initial-fix-wars-were-still-too-late-too-short-or-too-low-impact).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6039+) **Space victory denial now starts before the final launch window when parts are already high:** After KI#184 made AIs react faster and harder to immediate Space-win threats, BBAI follow-up logs showed that some Space rivals were sometimes still too close to winning before the countdown response began. In save file 450, Arabia still won because its recent war with Hannibal, the strongest nearby threat, had ended in normal Civ4 forced peace, temporarily preventing Hannibal from immediately restarting the war; by the time another anti-Space war could happen, Arabia was already at countdown 4. Save file 452 showed why this was not only a forced-peace edge case: Churchill's fast Space race was already dangerous while still pre-countdown / stage 3, so the KI#184 countdown/stage-4 response had not yet become strong enough. So Stage-3 Space leaders now also receive earlier utility pressure, direct-war consideration, and peace refusal once their spaceship is sufficiently complete and they are close enough to the spaceship-parts leader. In save file 452, Churchill still won, but was attacked around the 8/16-parts point and lost Oxford next turn; in save file 450, the Ramesses branch won, but likewise triggered wars and peace blocking at 8/16 parts, with later direct wars and cities changing hands. This is meant to start real pressure before the countdown, not to dogpile every Apollo builder. See [KI#184.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1842---fixedimproved-uwai-space-victory-denial-could-still-start-too-late-when-stage-3-space-leaders-already-had-many-spaceship-parts-before-countdown).
 - **Cultural-victory AI is viability and bottleneck-focused:** The new `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` BBAI logging showed Base AdvCiv could treat an AI raising the culture slider only for happiness or border pressure as evidence that it was pursuing a cultural victory. Even the early preparation stage could then raise culture priorities in every city. As a result, the AI could spend production, specialists, and commerce on cities culturally ranked lower than the cultural-victory target group (i.e., the top 3 cities that must reach Legendary culture), on a target city already much closer to Legendary than another target city, or even on a city that had already become Legendary. This was inefficient and could leave the AI dangerously underinvested in stronger economic, scientific, or military priorities. To address these issues, the AI no longer treats its culture slider alone as a cultural-victory commitment, and early preparation no longer raises culture priority throughout the empire. Before serious cultural victory pursuit begins, at least 2 of the 3 target cities must now each have already accumulated a tunable share of the Legendary requirement (10% by default), and the AI must rank among the configured number of leading cultural contenders (No point pursuing culture if we won't win culturally anyway). Once committed, only the target cities receive victory-specific culture weight, shifted toward the city projected to take longest (no point having a city have 70% legendary culture and another 10% legendary culture only, as several legendary cities are required to win culturally, so have the spread be more even); a city that is already Legendary keeps only independent local-border value. Converting production to culture remains available for first-ring expansion and strongly contested borders, but otherwise only to active target cities.
 - **Hopeless late cultural pursuits are abandoned:** The new `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` BBAI logging also showed a late cultural pursuit in which the least advanced target city was projected hundreds of turns from Legendary when the estimated game had little more than 100 turns remaining (e.g., Future Era at T~400 at Normal game speed), despite likely faster Space or other victory routes. The AI now returns to preparation when its maximum affordable culture-slider projection misses the estimated deadline beyond the tunable grace or falls too far behind competing cultural contenders, freeing resources for stronger victory routes.
